# Title: Winrs Local Command Execution
# ID: bcfece3d-56fe-4545-9931-3b8e92927db1
# Status: experimental
# Level: high
# Author: Liran Ravich, Nasreddine Bencherchali
# Date: 2025-10-22
# Tags: attack.lateral-movement, attack.stealth, attack.t1021.006, attack.t1218
# Description: Detects the execution of Winrs.exe where it is used to execute commands locally.
# Commands executed this way are launched under Winrshost.exe and can represent proxy execution used for defense evasion or lateral movement.
# Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

((((process.executable:*\\winrs.exe) OR (process.pe.original_file_name:"winrs.exe")) AND ((process.command_line:*/r:localhost* OR process.command_line:*-r:localhost* OR process.command_line:*/r:127.0.0.1* OR process.command_line:*-r:127.0.0.1* OR process.command_line:*/r:[::1]* OR process.command_line:*-r:[::1]* OR process.command_line:*/remote:localhost* OR process.command_line:*-remote:localhost* OR process.command_line:*/remote:127.0.0.1* OR process.command_line:*-remote:127.0.0.1* OR process.command_line:*/remote:[::1]* OR process.command_line:*-remote:[::1]*))) OR (((process.executable:*\\winrs.exe) OR (process.pe.original_file_name:"winrs.exe")) AND NOT (((process.command_line:*/r:* OR process.command_line:*-r:* OR process.command_line:*/remote:* OR process.command_line:*-remote:*)))))
